# OpenPass Browser Extension — NO runtime environment variables (by design)
#
# Browser extensions cannot read .env files at runtime, and OpenPass does not
# bake any configuration into the extension bundle. This file exists so the
# convention is explicit across all components.
#
# Where configuration actually lives:
# - Server URL + email: entered in the extension popup, stored in
#   chrome.storage.local under "openpass.serverUrl" / "openpass.email"
# - Device ID: generated once, stored in chrome.storage.local ("openpass.deviceId")
# - Vault keys / session tokens: popup memory ONLY — never persisted, and
#   closing the popup locks the extension.
#
# Build (no env needed):
#   bun run build           # Chrome  -> dist/
#   bun run build:firefox   # Firefox -> dist-firefox/
# The build copies the shared WASM crypto core from apps/web/src/lib/wasm.
